                    *************** 1.0 ***************
                        Installing "Dragon's Lord"

UnLHA the file DL1xxxx.LHA to your PFILES: directory.
(In Shell, in proper dir type: LHA x <filename> TO pfiles: )

This should create a directory called DL in your PFILES directory.

Go into CNet, and add a new Item, PICK AREXX for the game.
Set up the path, and everything else by using PFILES:DL/DL.rexx

THATS IT!


                    *************** 1.1 ***************
                     What Is Required To Run This Game

First, you MUST have CNet BBS software. This game has been tested on the
following versions of CNet: 2.63, 3.05c, 4.13f

It is assumed it should be compatably with any other versions. If for some
reason you have problems that you feel may be related to your version of
CNet, please email me and let me know the problem(s).

Next, you'll need the command 'copy' & 'delete' in your c: directory.

The amount of memory it takes to run this game varies depending on how many
people at the same time will be playing it. It will take roughly 100k per
port.

The amount of space on your HD needed for this game also varies according
to how many people you have playing it vs. how much the game is played. If
you have many players create a lot of characters, it will take less than
those who create one character for themselves. The base amount of space
(for just the program and its required files) is roughly 150k. Each player
datafile should run between 50 and 500 bytes. (ie, 10 maxed out users would
take up roughly 5k of disk space.) Usually this size is _much_ smaller than
500 bytes. It usually ranges in the 100 byte area.

You will also need RexxMast, which is a commercial program. If you don't
have this, you might have a slight problem running an ARexx program. ;)

If you have any questions about getting this program to work, email me.
(see below for my address(s).)


                    *************** 1.2 ***************
             How to Update Dragon's Lord From An Older Version

Follow the guide below on what to do as opposed to the new version:

v1.00g1 through v1.00g2:
        Delete the following Directories:
        dl/cave         dl/data         dl/info         dl/magi
        dl/mons         dl/text

        Delete the following Files:
        dl/dl.rexx      dl/char.reg     dl/Updates      dl/README.FIRST!

        Copy All Files in Archive into your Old DL/ Directory.
        *** You should retain old user files, ie, no need
        to restart the players, or delete the player files.


